# Where the owner-only read of GitHub text is stated or relied on (docs/standards/architecture.md
# rule 9; #720). The rule is docs/standards/security.md rule 6, which the claim cites; check-ledgers
# has no cite key, so the citation lives here.
owner: .claude/scripts/gh-owner-comments.sh
claim: the workflow reads an issue's or PR's text through gh-owner-comments.sh, which keeps only what the repository owner's account wrote, and non-owner text is data (security.md rule 6; #720)
sweep: gh-owner-comments\.(sh|mjs)
scope: :!docs/tech-debt.md :!docs/friction-log.md :!docs/review-feedback.md
carrier: .claude/agents/task-orchestrator.md
carrier: .claude/agents/ticket-agent.md
carrier: .claude/agents/untrusted-reader.md
carrier: .claude/skills/execute/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/skills/plan-issue/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/skills/retro/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/skills/run-issue/SKILL.md
carrier: docs/standards/security.md
excluded: .claude/scripts/gh-owner-comments.mjs
excluded: .claude/scripts/gh-owner-comments.test.sh
